.TH MUSIC-PLAYER 1 "August 2026" "music-player 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
music-player \- play music in a terminal interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B music-player
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B music-player
recursively scans the given directory for supported audio files and displays
them in a terminal interface. If no directory is supplied, it scans the
current directory. Audio playback is provided by
.BR ffplay (1).
.PP
Supported filename extensions are mp3, flac, wav, ogg, opus, m4a, and aac.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Up , Down , k , j
Select a track.
.TP
.B Enter
Play the selected track.
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume playback.
.TP
.B s
Stop playback.
.TP
.BR n , p
Play the next or previous track.
.TP
.BR q , Escape
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/ffplay
Required playback program.
